@startuml system-workflow
title ABAP LLM Wiki — Workflow (a meeting transcript becomes queryable knowledge)

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam ArrowFontColor #333333
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF7E0
skinparam NoteBorderColor #E0C46C

actor "Team member" as User

participant "OneDrive Inbox" as OD #E8F5E9
participant "Power Automate" as PA #E3F2FD
database "abap-wiki repo\n(pages · rules · raw/)" as REPO #ECEFF1
participant "GitHub Actions" as GHA #FFF3E0
participant "Ingest Script" as PY #F3E5F5
boundary "Claude API\n(claude-opus-4-8)" as CLAUDE #ECEFF1
participant "Obsidian\n(local clone)" as OBS #E8F5E9
participant "Claude Code" as CC #E3F2FD

User -> OD : 1. drops **OTC workshop transcript.pdf**

== Step 1 — The bridge carries the file to GitHub ==
OD -> PA : "file created" trigger
activate PA
PA -> OD : get file content
OD --> PA : PDF (2.4 MB)
PA -> REPO : HTTPS PUT → **raw/inbox/** (base64, PAT)
PA -> OD : move source → **inbox/sent** ("picked up")
deactivate PA
REPO --> REPO : commit lands = **push event**

== Step 2 — The robot wakes up and reads the document ==
REPO -> GHA : push touched raw/inbox/** → trigger
activate GHA
GHA -> PY : checkout vault, run **abap-ingest.py**
activate PY
PY -> PY : extract text (pdfplumber),\ndedup check vs **meta/inbox.md**

== Step 3 — Claude turns the transcript into wiki pages ==
PY -> PY : load **CLAUDE.md** rules + vault index
PY -> CLAUDE : rules + context + document text
activate CLAUDE
CLAUDE --> PY : **page operations**\n(3 updates + 1 new decision page)
deactivate CLAUDE
PY -> PY : write pages, append **meta/log.md**,\narchive source to raw/processed/
PY -> REPO : commit & push **vault updates**
deactivate PY
deactivate GHA

== Step 4 — The team syncs and reviews ==
REPO -> OBS : git pull (5-minute auto-sync)
OBS -> OBS : curator skims AI-written pages,\nfixes one name
OBS -> REPO : git push the **curator's fix**

== Step 5 — Anyone can ask the wiki ==
User -> CC : "What did we decide about the custom BAPI approach?"
activate CC
CC -> OBS : read pages + CLAUDE.md\n(from the same local clone)
OBS --> CC : **Decision page** + linked notes
CC -> CLAUDE : synthesize a cited answer
activate CLAUDE
CLAUDE --> CC : answer + citations
deactivate CLAUDE
CC --> User : 📄 **cited answer**\n("Approved 2026-07-15 — see the Decision page")
deactivate CC

note across
  One small bridge holds the system together: Power Automate makes a single
  authenticated HTTPS PUT into raw/inbox/ — the only link between Microsoft 365
  and GitHub. The commit itself triggers everything downstream, and one
  API-key-secured call to Claude does the librarian work. Humans only ever
  touch the wiki through Git sync and plain-English questions.
end note

@enduml
